  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Errors of the Amanuensis: or the Calumny of the Secretary is a story about an impertinent secretary using simple text and binary code. Each page includes a 'big word' that is slightly familiar but which most of us could not exactly define. That word, in caps, is illustrated by its translation into binary code. A take off of the 'For Dummies' series of books is tucked into the back cover decoding the message."--Women's Studio website, http://www.wsworkshop.org/  viewed October 13, 2010.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"A piece of KaKeART".</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Book explores the relationship between letterpress printing and binary code.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in an edition of 30 copies.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The artists' book "Transatlantic Balderdash" was created in 2010 by the artists as an accompaniment to "Errors of the amanuensis."</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The book was letterpress printed in Germany during an artist's residency at the Hessischisse Landes Museum für Industrie und Kultur.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">A small manual is placed in a pocket located on the inside back cover.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LC copy is number 11 of 30, signed by the authors.</subfield>
    <subfield code="5">DLC</subfield>
  </datafield>
